            {
                "content": "# SANTA YNEZ RIVER BASIN\n\n# 1260, Santa Ynez River near Santa Ynez, Calif.\n\nLocation. Lat 34\u00b035'30\" long 119\u00b059'45\" on boundary between Canada de los Pinos and Lomas de la Purification Grants on right bank, 1.1 miles downstream from Cachuma Dam and 5 miles southeast of Santa Ynez, Santa Barbara County.\n\nDrainage area 422 sq mi.\n\nRecords available -December 1928 to September 1931, October 1932 to September 1959.\n\nGage Water-stage recorder. Altitude of gage is 525 ft (from topographic map) Prior to Oct. 1, 1955, at site 2,1 miles downstream at different datum.\n\nExtremes Maximum discharge during year, 444 cfs Jan. 8 (gage height, 4.02 ft); no flow for many days 1928-31, 1932-59; Maximum discharge, 43,700 cfs Mar. 2, 1938 (gage height, 17.90 ft, site and datum then in use) from rating curve extended above float measurement of 34,100 cfs; no flow at times in some years.\n\nRemarks -Records good. Flow regulated by Jameson Lake and Gibralter and Cachuma Reser- voirs (see p. 189, 190, 195). Water diverted out of basin from Jameson Lake and Gib- ralter and Cachuma Reservoirs to cities of Montecito and Santa Barbara for municipal supply. Some water pumped from wells along river banks for irrigation.",
